# Scratch queue rows RFX (plan_process_overhaul.md P2.1). Data: the queue table in scratch_queue.md is generated
# from this file (python3 tools/status_index.py). Format: tools/scratch_query/qrows.py docstring.
# Run: qrun.py run OUT feature_writeup/testing/rows/RFX.qb RES [--section KEY] [--rows ID,...]

@@section 1
@@title SQ-RFX Rules fixes P3a: namespace binding, dict keys, moved tags and trades, 2026-11-17 ([plan_rules_fixes.md](../plan_rules_fixes.md) sections 6, 7, 12, 12b, 12c; TODO `conventions #17`, `#18`, `#23`, `#24`, `#25`)
@@date 2026-11-17
@@reviewed 2026-11-17
@@jars creativecommon creativecompat creativedevtools creativeengineering creativeequipment creativelabels creativeloot creativemagic creativeworldgen
@@sources kubejs/server_scripts kubejs/data/creativecompat/kubejs kubejs/data/creativemagic/kubejs kubejs/data/creativelabels/kubejs kubejs/data/creativeloot/kubejs kubejs/data/creativecommon/kubejs/tags kubejs/data/creativeequipment/kubejs/tags development/creativeCommon/src/main/resources/kubejs_startup/creativecommon/_lib tools/dump_diff.py
@@text
@@text Same content expected: recipes, tags and trades must equal the pre-change dumps except the listed moves. Baseline: `kubejs/exported/baseline_rules_p3a_2026-11-17/` in the instance (the 2026-11-15 `/dumpall` `recipes/`, `tags/`, `villager_trades.json`, `names.json`, copied before any P3a jar ran). It predates P2 and P2b (2026-11-17), so their own changes can also show (P2: tilled end stone tags, SQ-DRK-08); the exact pre-change state is commit 86659cfc with the jars `installToMods` moved to `jar_archive/displaced/` on 2026-11-17. Run SQ-RFX-01 before any `/reload`. Needs the P3a jars of 2026-11-17 (`creativecommon-1.2.0`, `creativecompat`, `creativemagic`, `creativeLabels-1.0.1`, `creativeequipment`, `creativedevtools`, `creativeworldgen`, `creativeloot` 1.0.0, `creativeengineering-2.0.0`, stamp `91d2ffb5`).
@@table
## SQ-RFX-01 | boot: the moved scripts load from their jars, no binding error
@group A
@commands Boot on the installed jars; read the KubeJS server log and latest.log
@pass `Dragon breathing starting` and `done`, `creative labels starting` and `done` in the server log; `[itemMerges] pack: N merges` with N two more than before (Little Logistics receiver and transmitter components into the Redstone Link); no `forPack: invalid`, no `ReferenceError`, no `is not defined` from a moved file (`dragon_breathing.js`, `creative_labels.js`, `botany_pots.js`, `wthittags.js`, `build_grid.js`, `equipmenttags.js`, `trades.js`)
@fails A moved file missing: its jar did not copy the tree (Labels: `build.gradle` script copy step; `jar` task checks it). `ReferenceError`: a dict alias used outside the callback that binds it (literal_id_swap.py places keys by the file's binding)
kjsexpect Dragon breathing done
kjsexpect creative labels done
kjsexpect \[itemMerges\] pack: \d+ merges
kjsreject forPack: invalid|ReferenceError|is not defined|global\.CDV\.buildGrid|tuneBase is not a function
shell grep -hE '\[itemMerges\] (pack|[0-9]+ pack)' logs/kubejs/server.log logs/kubejs/startup.log | tail -3
## SQ-RFX-02 | recipe ids: count unchanged, moves exactly the Compat, Magic and Labels sets
@group A
@commands `/dumpall`; `python3 $INST/tools/dump_diff.py recipes $INST/kubejs/exported/baseline_rules_p3a_2026-11-17 kubejs/exported --move creativeengineering=creativecompat --move creativeengineering=creativemagic --move creativeengineering=creativelabels`
@pass `RECIPES_SAME` (same count, no unexplained id); `moved creativeengineering -> creativecompat` about 380 (feature ports 377, misc mods, flower pots, the Fertile Soil pot soil), `-> creativemagic: 14` (dragon breathing), `-> creativelabels: 7` (3 shaped, 4 note specials); Equipment, Devtools, Worldgen, Loot and Engineering ids unchanged (they were already bound by their `recipes(...)` wrappers)
@fails `ONLY_BASE`/`ONLY_NEW` lines name the ids: a recipe file missed its `forPack` (namespace_lint.py), or a P2/P2b change since the 2026-11-15 baseline (check against commit 86659cfc before blaming P3a). A count change: a `global.has` guard or a dict key that resolves to nothing (`literal_id_swap.py`)
> dumpall
waitlog \[dumpall\] (all \d+ dumps done|\d+/\d+ (dumps )?ok) 900
shell python3 "$INST/tools/dump_diff.py" recipes "$INST/kubejs/exported/baseline_rules_p3a_2026-11-17" kubejs/exported --move creativeengineering=creativecompat --move creativeengineering=creativemagic --move creativeengineering=creativelabels | grep -vE '^(ONLY_|moved)' ; python3 "$INST/tools/dump_diff.py" recipes "$INST/kubejs/exported/baseline_rules_p3a_2026-11-17" kubejs/exported --move creativeengineering=creativecompat --move creativeengineering=creativemagic --move creativeengineering=creativelabels | grep -E '^(ONLY_|moved)' | head -40
look moved counts as in Pass; every ONLY_ line explained in the run doc
## SQ-RFX-03 | tags: dump equal to the baseline after the loot tag rename
@group A
@commands Same `/dumpall` as SQ-RFX-02; `python3 $INST/tools/dump_diff.py tags $INST/kubejs/exported/baseline_rules_p3a_2026-11-17 kubejs/exported --rename creativeworldgen:loot/=creativeloot:loot/`
@pass `TAGS_SAME`: the mining tags of Layered Obsidian, the Weathered Cardboard Box and the 10 coil blocks (from the builders' `tagBlock` to the tag scripts, V-32), the Creative Compat BlockRunner hook tags, `creativeequipment:bottled_air/fire_sources` and the WTHIT Silk Touch tags (into their jars, V-41) and the 611 swapped literals change nothing
@fails The listed tag shows the missing or extra member: `t.mineable` call in `server_scripts/tags/blocktags.js`, Compat's `tags/blocktags.js` or Engineering's `tags/storageblocktags.js`; a WTHIT tag empty: Common's jar has no `data/creativecommon/kubejs/tags/wthittags.js`. Tilled end stone differences are P2 (SQ-DRK-08)
shell python3 "$INST/tools/dump_diff.py" tags "$INST/kubejs/exported/baseline_rules_p3a_2026-11-17" kubejs/exported --rename creativeworldgen:loot/=creativeloot:loot/ | tail -40
## SQ-RFX-04 | villager trades: the pack-folder trades unchanged through global.trades.villager
@group A
@commands Same `/dumpall` (it runs `/dumptrades`); `python3 $INST/tools/dump_diff.py trades $INST/kubejs/exported/baseline_rules_p3a_2026-11-17 kubejs/exported dynamicvillage:mechanical_engineer dynamicvillage:hydraulic_engineer chefsdelight:delightchef minecraft:cleric`
@pass `TRADES_SAME`; no `global.trades.villager:` warning in the server log
@fails A profession differs: the converted row in `server_scripts/economy/trades.js` (count, uses, xp, price multiplier) or a rejected item (`global.trades.villager: ... is not an item_dict key`, `_validItem`)
shell python3 "$INST/tools/dump_diff.py" trades "$INST/kubejs/exported/baseline_rules_p3a_2026-11-17" kubejs/exported dynamicvillage:mechanical_engineer dynamicvillage:hydraulic_engineer chefsdelight:delightchef minecraft:cleric
kjsreject global\.trades\.villager:
## SQ-RFX-05 | LootJS names: CL/ for Creative Loot, CCM/ for the item merges
@group A
@commands Uncomment `event.enableLogging()` in the server's `kubejs/data/creativeloot/kubejs/loot/99_debug.js`, `/reload`, roll a village plains house chest 3 times; read latest.log
@pass `[LootJS]` lines name `CL/tuning`, `CL/removals/village_botania_cc` and `CCM/item_merges/pack`; none name `CE/loot/` or `CE/item_merges/`
@fails Old names: the pack-folder copy of `05_tuning.js` / `10_removals.js` or Common's `item_merges.js` is older than 2026-11-17; no `[LootJS]` lines: logging not on (the edit did not reach the script the server loads)
shell sed -i 's#^\(\s*\)// event.enableLogging()#\1event.enableLogging()#' kubejs/data/creativeloot/kubejs/loot/99_debug.js 2>/dev/null; grep -c 'event.enableLogging()' kubejs/data/creativeloot/kubejs/loot/99_debug.js || true
> reload
waitlog Reloaded|reload 180
> forceload add 3200 3200 3216 3216
> fill 3200 -60 3200 3210 -50 3210 minecraft:air
repeat 3
> loot spawn 3205 -58 3205 loot minecraft:chests/village/village_plains_house
end
sleep 2
shell grep -oE '(CL|CCM|CE)/[a-z_/]+' logs/latest.log | sort | uniq -c
expect CL/tuning
expect CCM/item_merges/pack
reject CE/(loot|item_merges)/
look `CL/removals/village_botania_cc` appears when a roll had a Botania or CC:Tweaked stack to remove (it may not in 3 rolls)
